{
  "dom_id": "step-q89992",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt{4-5x}+10.$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4-5x}+10=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4-5x}+10 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{4-5x} & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no roots.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
